=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  |\n|  | {{field-3}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, since ${v}_{1}+{v}_{2}=0,$ we have that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{v}_{1}-7{v}_{2} & =13{v}_{1}-7{v}_{1}-7{v}_{2} \\\\  & =13{v}_{1}-7({v}_{1}+{v}_{2}) \\\\  & =13{v}_{1}-7(0) \\\\  & =13{v}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nT(6{v}_{1}-7{v}_{2})=T(13{v}_{1}).\n$$\n\nNow, since $T$ is a linear transformation, we have that $T(kv)=kT(v).$ So \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(13{v}_{1}) & =13T({v}_{1}) \\\\  & =13[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}52 \\\\ -13 \\\\ 39\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn conclusion, $T(6{v}_{1}-7{v}_{2})=[\\begin{aligned}52 \\\\ -13 \\\\ 39\\end{aligned}].$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-317833/field-1" "q-317833/field-2" "q-317833/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9fbd335c-28cc-5f02-b773-f685e8b15417"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-317833"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-8297/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "7941cea8-77d1-5b7d-9cfe-e8249608fba6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8297/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "dfdde30a-eeef-54d3-9b1a-8b10680a03c2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8297/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "786814a1-c5d9-528f-b248-06eb8742fd48" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8297/selection/93198c2e65472148f49c73a47d70892e6efd0b46acbb489ee2afeea42a4a8c25" :answer/id #uuid "114f1c3c-ef33-530d-ae82-d223910a8968" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8297/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" :answer/id #uuid "4295c50f-f640-540a-a2dc-97b5442319e9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8297/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "cde7384a-9338-5e1d-b03c-f33c1d244093" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-8297/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" :answer-field/choices ["q-8297/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-8297/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-8297/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-8297/selection/93198c2e65472148f49c73a47d70892e6efd0b46acbb489ee2afeea42a4a8c25" "q-8297/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-8297" :question/id #uuid "0394caee-e965-5b6f-91aa-7fb8f0bbd3b6" :question/math-academy-id "q-8297" :question/problem "Let \n$T:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}3y \\\\ 2x\\end{aligned}].$\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $T(kv)=kT(v)$ for any real $2\\times 1$ column vector $v$ and real scalar $k$\n- $T({v}_{1}+{v}_{2})=T({v}_{1})+T({v}_{2})$ for any real $2\\times 1$ column vectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$\n- $T$ is a linear transformation" :question/worked-solution "A linear transformation $T$ satisfies two properties:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & T[\\begin{aligned}kx \\\\ ky\\end{aligned}]=kT[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}], \\\\  & T[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}+{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}]=T[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+T[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Checking the first condition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T[\\begin{aligned}kx \\\\ ky\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3ky \\\\ 2kx\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =k[\\begin{aligned}3y \\\\ 2x\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =kT[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}].\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Checking the second condition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}+{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3({y}_{1}+{y}_{2}) \\\\ 2({x}_{1}+{x}_{2})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3{y}_{1} \\\\ 2{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3{y}_{2} \\\\ 2{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =T[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+T[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\text{T}$ is a linear transformation.\n\nAs a result, all three statements are true." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-8297/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d8c04b23-e341-57e9-a072-985e4b536e5a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-8297"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-12008/selection/93198c2e65472148f49c73a47d70892e6efd0b46acbb489ee2afeea42a4a8c25" :answer/id #uuid "c2bcc7a1-19ed-5439-9594-9c60437fac16" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-12008/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "70355b54-e5e3-58fa-ab81-fb569f95146a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-12008/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" :answer/id #uuid "c8532f2a-0470-5497-9a97-ae414dd1060d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-12008/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "64acbc19-30c2-5c17-9f51-838f600343d1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/val